WEBVTT

00:45.333 --> 00:47.249
We are here with Verity Crawford

00:47.250 --> 00:48.665
at her home in Vermont,

00:48.666 --> 00:51.374
the place she shares with
her husband and the twins.

00:51.375 --> 00:53.540
I don't think there
are enough superlatives

00:53.541 --> 00:55.582
to describe this woman.
Let's pick one.

00:55.583 --> 00:59.582
Phenomenon, sensation, marvel.

00:59.583 --> 01:02.707
Uh, some would say "badass."
I'll go with that.

01:02.708 --> 01:05.332
You are considered one
of the bestselling authors

01:05.333 --> 01:06.499
on the planet.

01:06.500 --> 01:07.624
- Oh...
- Let's take that in

01:07.625 --> 01:08.749
for just a second.

01:08.750 --> 01:10.082
- "On the planet."
- Yes.

01:10.083 --> 01:12.540
Have you had time
to take it all in? What it...

01:12.541 --> 01:14.415
What it is like
to be able to provide

01:14.416 --> 01:17.124
such a beautiful life for
the people you love so much?

01:17.125 --> 01:20.624
To me, it's all a miracle.

01:20.625 --> 01:22.749
Yeah, but some could say...

01:22.750 --> 01:25.207
it's a miracle
built on villains.

02:06.041 --> 02:07.457
"I don't know that anyone

02:07.458 --> 02:09.165
"named Louie Longsutter

02:09.166 --> 02:11.415
"could even be dangerous.

02:11.416 --> 02:13.790
"But the way he stands there

02:13.791 --> 02:16.957
"just a little too close
to the edge of the porch,

02:16.958 --> 02:18.290
"like he's been waiting for me

02:18.291 --> 02:19.665
"longer than he should have

02:19.666 --> 02:22.749
"makes me second-guess
my assumptions.

02:22.750 --> 02:27.124
"I try to imagine a serial
killer named Louie Longsutter.

02:27.125 --> 02:28.999
"I almost laugh
at the absurdity of it,

02:29.000 --> 02:30.707
"but being a woman

02:30.708 --> 02:33.749
"about to embark
on weeks of isolation,

02:33.750 --> 02:36.415
"the thought that he could
be a threat sticks in my mind.

02:36.416 --> 02:38.499
"Unwanted and uncomfortable."

02:41.333 --> 02:42.707
Sorry. Sorry.

02:42.708 --> 02:43.874
Sorry.

02:43.875 --> 02:46.165
Hi, hi.
No, I'm in a bookstore.

02:46.166 --> 02:47.708
Yeah, yeah, this is a good time.

02:50.708 --> 02:52.832
- <i>Hey.</i>
- Hey. How'd it go?

02:52.833 --> 02:54.499
I don't want to talk about it.

02:54.500 --> 02:56.415
Where were you? You said
you were gonna be here.

02:56.416 --> 02:57.665
<i>You know I wouldn't miss it</i>

02:57.666 --> 02:59.915
<i>if I didn't have a good reason.</i>

02:59.916 --> 03:02.374
Hachette Book Group called.

03:02.375 --> 03:03.707
They wanna meet you.

03:03.708 --> 03:06.332
For what? Who... Who...
Who wants to meet me?

03:06.333 --> 03:07.707
<i>They wouldn't say.</i>

03:07.708 --> 03:09.500
It's all very top secret.

03:10.166 --> 03:11.332
When?

03:11.333 --> 03:13.290
3:00 p.m. sharp.

03:13.291 --> 03:14.499
I'll meet you there, okay?

03:14.500 --> 03:16.624
Oh, please, and dress nice.

03:16.625 --> 03:18.499
<i>All right?</i>

03:18.500 --> 03:19.750
Wait, Corey.

03:21.666 --> 03:22.915
Wow.

03:33.750 --> 03:36.708
<i>People like me belong
in overpopulated cities.</i>

03:41.583 --> 03:44.707
<i>In the tiny town
where I grew up,</i>

03:44.708 --> 03:47.041
<i>everyone knew
everything about everyone.</i>

03:51.958 --> 03:53.958
<i>But here, I'm invisible.</i>

03:57.833 --> 03:59.208
<i>I like it that way.</i>

04:09.041 --> 04:10.207
Yo, mister, watch out!

04:15.166 --> 04:17.874
Oh, my God!
Oh, my God!

04:17.875 --> 04:19.082
A man was riding his bike...

04:19.083 --> 04:20.499
- He's not good.
- Hey?

04:20.500 --> 04:22.207
And a car
just came out of nowhere,

04:22.208 --> 04:23.416
- and it hit him.
- Oh, my God.

04:25.208 --> 04:27.165
Oh, no.

04:27.166 --> 04:28.624
There's been
a terrible accident.

04:28.625 --> 04:32.082
A bike messenger
was hit by a car.

04:40.250 --> 04:41.250
Are you hurt?

04:43.500 --> 04:45.874
Are you hurt?

04:45.875 --> 04:47.458
Is it on my face?

04:50.666 --> 04:51.999
There should be a bathroom
in this coffee shop

04:52.000 --> 04:53.332
over here, okay?

04:53.333 --> 04:54.958
Look what you did!

05:03.250 --> 05:05.540
Oh...

05:05.541 --> 05:07.708
Hey, what are you doin'
in there? It's the men's room.

05:09.041 --> 05:10.291
We'll be right out.

05:31.750 --> 05:33.333
Here, um...

05:34.125 --> 05:35.125
you can put this on.

05:37.291 --> 05:38.707
Thank you.

05:38.708 --> 05:39.708
Of course.

05:44.958 --> 05:47.375
I can't tell
if you're calm or...

05:48.083 --> 05:49.250
if you're in shock.

05:51.750 --> 05:53.250
I don't know what I am.

05:57.583 --> 06:00.249
Are you okay?

06:00.250 --> 06:02.624
Uh, yeah.

06:02.625 --> 06:04.875
I've seen worse, unfortunately.

06:06.125 --> 06:07.416
Are you a doctor?

06:08.791 --> 06:10.291
I'm in real estate.

06:13.166 --> 06:14.833
Or at least, I used to be.

06:17.083 --> 06:18.458
What happened to you?

06:21.041 --> 06:22.625
You really wanna know?

06:28.541 --> 06:30.124
I pulled my 8-year-old
daughter's body

06:30.125 --> 06:32.458
out of a lake last spring.

06:39.208 --> 06:40.791
I'm sorry.

06:42.708 --> 06:44.208
I'm sorry.

06:47.125 --> 06:49.500
My mom died last week.

06:50.625 --> 06:52.082
Oh...

06:52.083 --> 06:53.832
What happened to her?

06:53.833 --> 06:55.374
Uh, cancer.

06:55.375 --> 06:58.082
I was taking care of her
in my apartment.

06:58.083 --> 06:59.457
She died in there.

06:59.458 --> 07:02.416
In my apartment.
She died. Sorry.

07:05.625 --> 07:07.124
I have a meeting. I should...

07:07.125 --> 07:09.125
Yeah, me, too.

07:10.250 --> 07:11.665
Thank you for your help.

07:11.666 --> 07:12.916
Of course.

07:19.416 --> 07:20.958
I'm Jeremy, by the way.

07:21.291 --> 07:22.500
Lowen.

07:35.333 --> 07:36.750
God.

07:42.416 --> 07:44.332
Congratulations on your bonus.

07:44.333 --> 07:45.333
Thank you.

07:53.791 --> 07:55.874
- Hi.
- Hi. How can I help you?

07:55.875 --> 07:57.290
I'm here to see Amanda Thomas.

07:57.291 --> 07:59.415
- Okay.
- Lowen.

07:59.416 --> 08:00.582
Hi. I'm sorry I'm late.

08:00.583 --> 08:02.666
You're not late.
You're on time.

08:03.916 --> 08:05.874
The actual meeting
isn't until 3:30.

08:05.875 --> 08:09.583
But I'd figured you'd be late,
as usual, so I told you 3:00.

08:10.000 --> 08:11.332
Sorry.

08:11.333 --> 08:13.207
If you had told me that,
I could have avoided...

08:13.208 --> 08:14.875
What are you wearing?

08:16.916 --> 08:18.165
Um...

08:18.166 --> 08:19.665
It's like a fashion thing.

08:19.666 --> 08:20.999
Corey. Lowen.

08:21.000 --> 08:23.000
I'm Amanda's assistant, Olivia.

08:23.791 --> 08:24.957
Thank you.

08:24.958 --> 08:26.398
I'll show you
to the conference room.

08:30.166 --> 08:31.500
You comin'?

08:35.125 --> 08:36.500
Oh, my God.

08:45.625 --> 08:46.708
Sorry about your mom.

08:48.083 --> 08:49.250
Don't be.

08:50.750 --> 08:52.457
Can I help with the will?

08:52.458 --> 08:54.540
I'm sure Edward can take a look.

08:54.541 --> 08:56.749
Mm, I don't need a lawyer.

08:56.750 --> 08:59.291
All she left me was debt.

08:59.833 --> 09:01.124
Showtime.

09:01.125 --> 09:02.249
Right this way.

09:02.250 --> 09:03.957
Oh...

09:05.500 --> 09:07.290
You must be Lowen Ashleigh.

09:07.291 --> 09:08.499
I am Amanda Thomas,

09:08.500 --> 09:10.249
Senior Editor here at Hachette.

09:10.250 --> 09:11.665
- Lowen.
- Nice to see you.

09:11.666 --> 09:12.915
Corey.

09:12.916 --> 09:14.124
This is
Barron Stephens, our lawyer,

09:14.125 --> 09:15.916
and Jeremy Crawford, our client.

09:20.166 --> 09:21.958
Please, have a seat.

09:28.791 --> 09:30.957
So I'll just cut to the chase.

09:30.958 --> 09:32.290
One of our authors

09:32.291 --> 09:34.249
is unable to fulfill a contract

09:34.250 --> 09:36.499
due to extenuating
circumstances.

09:36.500 --> 09:38.165
We are in search of a writer

09:38.166 --> 09:40.832
who has experience
with the same genre.

09:40.833 --> 09:42.749
She needs a little help.

09:42.750 --> 09:44.207
Before we continue, I would ask

09:44.208 --> 09:46.832
that you sign
the non-disclosure agreement.

09:46.833 --> 09:48.540
We would like to keep our
author's current situation

09:48.541 --> 09:50.625
out of the media.

10:01.166 --> 10:02.333
Thank you.

10:04.208 --> 10:06.958
Thank you, thank you.

10:09.500 --> 10:12.499
Verity Crawford is her name.

10:12.500 --> 10:15.582
I'm sure you're familiar
with her work.

10:15.583 --> 10:18.749
Verity has
a wildly successful series,

10:18.750 --> 10:20.040
<i>The Noble Virtues,</i>

10:20.041 --> 10:22.749
which we would hate
to see go unfinished.

10:22.750 --> 10:24.665
So we need a writer
who's able to step in

10:24.666 --> 10:26.457
on an accelerated timeline.

10:26.458 --> 10:27.790
So when will you need it by?

10:27.791 --> 10:29.249
Your wife?

10:29.250 --> 10:30.707
We're already behind,
so we're looking to have

10:30.708 --> 10:32.582
the next book in the series
within six months,

10:32.583 --> 10:35.582
and the final two
in the next 24 months.

10:35.583 --> 10:37.540
Three books.

10:37.541 --> 10:39.916
$75,000 per book.

10:42.750 --> 10:45.541
So how does this sound, Lowen?

10:46.958 --> 10:49.250
Um...

10:52.291 --> 10:55.624
I appreciate the offer.

10:55.625 --> 10:58.624
I don't know that I can write
for another author.

10:58.625 --> 11:00.707
I'm...

11:00.708 --> 11:03.791
Especially someone as popular
as Verity Crawford...

11:04.541 --> 11:08.124
Her fans know her voice.

11:08.125 --> 11:10.125
They would know it's not her.

11:11.833 --> 11:13.499
I'm sorry.

11:13.500 --> 11:15.124
Let me talk to my client.

11:15.125 --> 11:16.832
All right?

11:16.833 --> 11:18.957
We'll step out.

11:18.958 --> 11:20.207
We have
two other writers in mind.

11:20.208 --> 11:21.665
So if you could
let us know something

11:21.666 --> 11:23.332
by tomorrow afternoon?

11:23.333 --> 11:25.249
We'll discuss. All right?

11:25.250 --> 11:26.791
Thank you.

11:34.416 --> 11:36.500
Could we possibly
have a word in private?

11:39.625 --> 11:40.833
What the fuck?

11:41.958 --> 11:43.457
Fine.

11:43.458 --> 11:45.874
Sure.

11:45.875 --> 11:47.291
You got it.

11:52.083 --> 11:54.124
Are you okay?

11:54.125 --> 11:56.458
Twenty minutes ago,
you watched someone die.

11:58.125 --> 11:59.707
So did you.

11:59.708 --> 12:01.249
Like I said...

12:01.250 --> 12:02.750
I've seen worse.

12:05.375 --> 12:07.249
You must have questions.

12:07.250 --> 12:08.500
Sure do.

12:08.875 --> 12:09.999
Shoot.

12:10.000 --> 12:11.749
Okay, well, for starters,

12:11.750 --> 12:13.457
did you go shopping

12:13.458 --> 12:16.875
or do you carry around
spare shirts in your pocket?

12:20.250 --> 12:22.457
My hotel's
just around the corner.

12:22.458 --> 12:25.040
I went back and got changed.

12:25.041 --> 12:27.583
Why can't your wife
finish the series?

12:29.833 --> 12:31.958
Verity had a car accident.

12:34.458 --> 12:36.458
I'm sorry.

12:39.291 --> 12:40.916
<i>Open Ended.</i>

12:42.958 --> 12:45.583
It was one of Verity's
favorite books last year.

12:48.041 --> 12:49.457
She read one of my books?

12:49.458 --> 12:50.666
Yeah.

12:54.250 --> 12:57.624
She said
that you are a brilliant,

12:57.625 --> 13:00.332
undiscovered voice.

13:00.333 --> 13:02.374
Well, I'm not undiscovered.

13:02.375 --> 13:03.915
I am published.

13:03.916 --> 13:06.415
Just not in a big way.

13:06.416 --> 13:09.207
If anyone was to take over
her series,

13:09.208 --> 13:12.832
I wanted it to be someone
whose work she respected.

13:12.833 --> 13:15.665
You would have to spend
some time at the house.

13:15.666 --> 13:16.832
In her office.

13:16.833 --> 13:20.374
She has years of notes
and outlines,

13:20.375 --> 13:22.708
stuff I wouldn't know
how to make sense of.

13:23.666 --> 13:27.040
Also, they're lowballing you.

13:27.041 --> 13:30.541
You should ask your agent
to ask for half a million.

13:33.208 --> 13:34.707
We live in Vermont.

13:34.708 --> 13:37.166
You can stay
for as long as you need to.

13:38.041 --> 13:39.207
I hope you change your mind.

13:39.208 --> 13:40.957
Wait.

13:40.958 --> 13:44.541
Did you know who I was earlier?

13:46.333 --> 13:49.207
Not until you said your name.

13:49.208 --> 13:51.291
There aren't that many
Lowens running around.

13:53.541 --> 13:55.791
If you do come,
bring my shirt back.

14:01.333 --> 14:04.207
<i>Verity, welcome
to</i> Call Her Daddy.

14:04.208 --> 14:07.375
<i>Who doesn't love a dirty,
twisted thriller?</i>

14:08.708 --> 14:11.707
<i>Uh, maybe just my husband.</i>

14:11.708 --> 14:15.290
<i>Oh! Is it hard for him
to read your work</i>

14:15.291 --> 14:17.540
<i>and then sleep next to you
at night?</i>

14:18.791 --> 14:21.332
<i>I mean, your characters
are pretty evil.</i>

14:21.333 --> 14:23.290
<i>Yeah, well, yeah, well, um...</i>

14:23.291 --> 14:25.790
<i>um...</i>

14:25.791 --> 14:27.040
<i>he was wondering if I was</i>

14:27.041 --> 14:28.790
<i>like the sociopath
that was doing it.</i>

14:28.791 --> 14:30.915
<i>And I think he was
maybe just checking.</i>

14:30.916 --> 14:32.124
<i>- For sure.
- Just, like...</i>

14:32.125 --> 14:33.290
<i>- Who wouldn't?
- Let's just...</i>

14:33.291 --> 14:34.583
<i>You know.</i>

15:30.541 --> 15:32.915
Hope I'm not intruding.

15:32.916 --> 15:35.250
I'm here
to celebrate your new gig.

15:38.708 --> 15:39.791
You're moving?

15:40.916 --> 15:43.874
I can't live here anymore.

15:43.875 --> 15:47.540
I'm also getting evicted, so...

15:47.541 --> 15:50.624
- Uh...
- It all works out.

15:50.625 --> 15:54.207
Well, maybe with the money
you'll get from this deal,

15:54.208 --> 15:57.374
you'll finally get a cover
for that futon.

15:57.375 --> 15:59.249
Excuse me, that is not a futon.

15:59.250 --> 16:00.416
It's a mattress.

16:02.541 --> 16:03.958
Let's toast, yeah?

16:07.125 --> 16:09.207
Can't believe...

16:09.208 --> 16:11.915
you're staying at their house.

16:11.916 --> 16:15.957
There's, like, years' worth
of notes and outlines.

16:15.958 --> 16:17.165
Somebody
needs to sort through...

16:17.166 --> 16:18.250
You don't even know them.

16:20.875 --> 16:23.458
All I'm saying
is that you have to be safe.

16:28.708 --> 16:29.791
Cheers.

16:31.541 --> 16:33.125
Cheers.

16:37.166 --> 16:39.249
Have you even read
one of her books?

16:39.250 --> 16:42.333
I don't read books that you
can buy in an airport.

16:43.083 --> 16:44.207
I'm afraid I'll like it

16:44.208 --> 16:46.415
and then I won't be able
to resent her.

16:46.416 --> 16:49.207
Don't be fooled by her success.

16:49.208 --> 16:51.832
She's very, very dark.

16:51.833 --> 16:53.333
Like you.

16:56.416 --> 16:57.750
How's Becca?

16:59.083 --> 17:00.457
Who's Becca?

17:00.458 --> 17:03.333
There's pictures of you guys
all over Instagram.

17:03.958 --> 17:06.290
It's just a fling.

17:06.291 --> 17:08.625
She looks sweet.

17:09.875 --> 17:12.333
You should take that seriously.

17:24.500 --> 17:26.041
Okay.

17:28.583 --> 17:30.875
I'm happy for you, Lowen.

17:31.875 --> 17:33.041
You deserve this.

17:41.125 --> 17:43.124
<i>"I reach the door..."</i>

17:43.125 --> 17:45.000
<i>"push it open without knocking.</i>

17:46.333 --> 17:49.499
<i>"I smell the blood
before I see it.</i>

17:49.500 --> 17:52.374
<i>"Lane is hunched over...</i>

17:52.375 --> 17:55.332
<i>"the knife stuck under his chin.</i>

17:55.333 --> 17:58.665
<i>"A steady flow of crimson
seeps through his knuckles,</i>

17:58.666 --> 18:01.332
<i>"pours down his arm.</i>

18:01.333 --> 18:03.749
<i>"He reaches out to me,</i>

18:03.750 --> 18:06.499
<i>"desperate for my help.</i>

18:06.500 --> 18:09.165
<i>"I meet him halfway</i>

18:09.166 --> 18:13.665
<i>"and use my palm
to push the knife in deeper.</i>

18:13.666 --> 18:15.999
<i>"I stare into his eyes,</i>

18:16.000 --> 18:19.208
<i>"wanting him to know
how much I enjoy this."</i>

18:59.666 --> 19:00.999
Hey, you made it.

19:01.000 --> 19:02.374
Hi.

19:02.375 --> 19:04.124
Uh, a little sooner
than we expected.

19:04.125 --> 19:05.290
Sorry.

19:05.291 --> 19:06.957
No, no, no, no. No.

19:06.958 --> 19:08.790
It's totally fine.

19:08.791 --> 19:10.958
This is who
I was talking about, buddy.

19:12.583 --> 19:15.457
I'm Lowen. What's your name?

19:15.458 --> 19:17.333
- I'm Crew.
- Hi, Crew.

19:19.541 --> 19:21.624
He's so cute.

19:21.625 --> 19:23.832
He's a little shy.

19:23.833 --> 19:25.250
That's okay.

19:26.250 --> 19:28.707
I'm a little shy, too.

19:28.708 --> 19:31.207
Come on in.
Let me take your bag.

19:31.208 --> 19:33.582
- Thank you.
- Of course.

20:14.833 --> 20:16.000
Pretty amazing, huh?

20:17.916 --> 20:19.125
Is that a field?

20:20.833 --> 20:21.958
It's a lake.

20:26.708 --> 20:28.499
Do you want me
to show your room?

20:28.500 --> 20:30.915
Or, I mean, are you hungry?
You must be.

20:30.916 --> 20:33.624
I mean, it's such
a long drive from the city.

20:33.625 --> 20:35.957
Crew and I are having PBJs
and sliced apples,

20:35.958 --> 20:37.707
if you want some.
I'm sure we can rustle up

20:37.708 --> 20:38.832
something
a little better, though.

20:38.833 --> 20:40.665
I'm okay. Thank you.

20:40.666 --> 20:41.999
Yeah?

20:42.000 --> 20:44.207
Okay. Well,
fridge is fully stocked.

20:44.208 --> 20:46.665
If you want anything,
just help yourself.

20:46.666 --> 20:48.124
Can I go see Mommy?

20:48.125 --> 20:49.290
Yeah, of course, buddy.

20:49.291 --> 20:51.000
Just go talk to Anna first,
all right?

20:55.833 --> 20:57.457
You get the main bedroom.

20:57.458 --> 20:59.040
I hope you don't mind.

20:59.041 --> 21:00.915
Um, we all sleep upstairs now,

21:00.916 --> 21:02.040
and so we just thought

21:02.041 --> 21:03.249
that this room would be best

21:03.250 --> 21:04.540
'cause it's closest
to Verity's office,

21:04.541 --> 21:06.333
which is just right down there.

21:07.666 --> 21:09.000
Okay.

21:10.083 --> 21:11.499
The bathroom is all yours.

21:11.500 --> 21:12.957
Uh, there should
be toiletries in there,

21:12.958 --> 21:14.874
but if there isn't,
just let me know

21:14.875 --> 21:16.708
and we can get
whatever you need.

21:19.583 --> 21:20.916
Wow.

21:21.375 --> 21:22.708
Thank you.

21:23.875 --> 21:26.082
Yep.

21:26.083 --> 21:28.957
So, do you want some time
to just, like, get settled

21:28.958 --> 21:31.541
or do you want me
to show you the office?

21:39.708 --> 21:41.541
- The office.
- Okay.

21:46.916 --> 21:49.832
She saved everything
on her computer,

21:49.833 --> 21:51.082
in boxes.

21:51.083 --> 21:53.207
There's no order to it, though.

21:53.208 --> 21:55.249
She wasn't the most
organized person.

21:55.250 --> 21:57.083
Most writers aren't.

22:00.125 --> 22:01.708
- Wow.
- Mm-hmm.

22:18.875 --> 22:20.291
Which one is your favorite?

22:22.166 --> 22:24.790
Honestly, I haven't read any
of them since the first one.

22:24.791 --> 22:26.540
I didn't like being in her head.

22:26.541 --> 22:29.415
Hmm. Can I meet her?

22:44.291 --> 22:46.415
Anna, this is Lowen Ashleigh,

22:46.416 --> 22:47.790
the author
I was telling you about.

22:47.791 --> 22:48.957
Hi, Crew.

22:48.958 --> 22:50.915
- Hi.
- Lowen,

22:50.916 --> 22:53.999
this is Anna, Verity's nurse.

22:54.000 --> 22:55.832
Hi. Nice to meet you.

22:55.833 --> 22:57.415
Hello, Lowen.

22:57.416 --> 22:59.290
Nice to meet you, too.

22:59.291 --> 23:00.791
I thought you'd be older.

23:02.125 --> 23:03.541
Is now a good time?

23:05.000 --> 23:07.166
We were just
about to take a walk.

23:10.416 --> 23:13.540
Verity, this is Lowen Ashleigh.

23:22.625 --> 23:25.750
Hi, Verity. How are you?

23:27.208 --> 23:29.041
How are you today, Verity?

23:31.708 --> 23:33.082
We're good.

23:33.083 --> 23:36.499
Took some meds
and ready for the fresh air.

23:36.500 --> 23:38.750
Okay. Should be
an easy evening then.

23:56.916 --> 23:58.750
Would you have come if you knew?

24:01.625 --> 24:02.865
We need to keep things close...

24:04.291 --> 24:05.790
because of the media.

24:05.791 --> 24:08.124
And if Hachette found out,
it would just be...

24:08.125 --> 24:10.249
There's no way
I can help her write.

24:10.250 --> 24:11.665
I... I can't.

24:11.666 --> 24:14.166
Verity was inspired
by your writing.

24:15.291 --> 24:18.207
You're the only writer
who can do this.

24:18.208 --> 24:19.375
I'm certain of it, Lowen.

24:41.666 --> 24:43.665
<i>Chapter after chapter
of intrigue</i>

24:43.666 --> 24:46.832
<i>and fucked-up characters.</i>

24:46.833 --> 24:48.250
<i>Really fucked-up characters.</i>

24:53.791 --> 24:57.208
<i>All her books are from
the villain's point of view.</i>

24:57.958 --> 24:59.791
<i>That's new to me.</i>
